mode: "100644"
text: "# Triage rules, scorecard + two worked examples\n\n## Keep / kill / refresh decision rules (signal-based)\n| Verdict | Signals | Action |\n|---|---|---|\n| **KEEP / scale** | above-median saves/shares + on-goal + on-brand | double down; add to recycle queue (`content-recycling`) |\n| **REFRESH / revive** | good idea but dated info, weak hook, underseen, or cross-posted/non-native | update hook/data/format + re-publish |\n| **KILL / cut** | chronic low saves/shares across reps, off-brand, dead format, misleading | stop making it; human approves any deletion |\n> **Refresh before kill.** Low *likes* alone is never the kill criterion — check saves/shares + the goal.\n> Don't auto-delete (evergreen/SEO value + engagement history).\n\n## Pillar-coverage map\nList your pillars → tally % of last-90-days posts per pillar → compare to intended mix. Flag\n**over-served** (cut back) and **under-served / whitespace** (a winning pillar starved of posts is the\nhighest-leverage fix). → `content-pillars`.\n\n## Voice-drift check (both directions)\n1. Do recent posts match `brand-profile`/`voice-builder`? (drifted off-brand → realign.)\n2. Are your **top performers** off the documented voice? (the voice may need to **evolve** toward what\n   works → update `voice-builder`.) Record which it is.\n\n## Profile-fundamentals checklist (compound, zero spend)\nBio clear + keyworded · links work + drive the right destination · **pinned/featured = current winners**\n· handle + visuals consistent across platforms · native formats used · contact/CTA present. → `profile-optimization`.\n\n## The audit scorecard (output)\n```\nSTRENGTHS: what's working (winning pillars/formats/times)\nWEAKNESSES: chronic losers, whitespace, voice drift, profile leaks\nOPPORTUNITIES: refresh candidates, under-served winning pillars, format shifts\nTRIAGE: keep[..] / refresh[..] / kill[..]\nROADMAP: quick wins (this week) vs long-term (this quarter) + owners + timelines\n```\n\n## Worked example 1 — busy-but-flat account (blunt indie-founder voice)\n```\nINVENTORY: 90 days, 78 posts, 3 platforms. PLAN: 2 pillars (tax tips, founder BTS).\nSIGNAL: top 10 by saves/reach = all \"one-rule\" tax Reels at 9am; bottom = reposted landscape clips.\nDIAGNOSE: tax pillar over-delivers, BTS starved (whitespace); cross-posted clips = non-native; bio link dead.\nTRIAGE: KEEP one-rule Reels; REFRESH the BTS angle into vertical; KILL landscape reposts. PROFILE: fix bio link, pin top Reel.\nROADMAP: quick win = fix link + pin today; long-term = 2 BTS Reels/wk. -> content-recycling, profile-optimization.\n```\n\n## Worked example 2 — voice-drift finding (warm studio voice)\n```\nFINDING: the 3 best-performing posts are warmer + more personal than the documented \"neutral professional\" voice.\nREAD: this is voice-evolution signal, not off-brand drift -> propose updating voice-builder toward the warmer tone.\nALSO: \"calm bookkeeping\" pillar is under-served despite strong saves -> rebalance (content-pillars).\nROADMAP: quick win = 2 warmer posts this week to confirm; long-term = revise voice guide + pillar mix.\n```\n\nBoth: read the plan + native analytics first; score on signal; refresh before kill; human approves\ndeletions; end in a quick-wins-vs-long-term roadmap that hands off — never a spreadsheet graveyard.\n"
